SWEET CHG P2 (patch 0284, charger bring-up phase 2, docs/research/charger-max77759-gs101.md section 8 steps 4-5, section 5.4): default-OFF (boot-arg sweetchgi2c=1) READ pass over the MAX77759 chips through HSI2C12 exactly as the bootloader left it (phase 1, patch 0283, observed SW_CONF=0x4, pads func 2 pull 3, CTL=0x48, CONF=0x980110ff auto mode, FS3 DIV 62, gates open: no bring-up writes). chg_i2c_read(slave, reg, n<=16) = two auto-mode messages (register address without STOP, then read n with STOP). HSI2C12 STORES (HW-WRITE, unreviewed, for the Opus reviewer): only CTL direction bits, FIFO_CTL, INT_ENABLE, INT_STATUS clear, AUTO_CONF, TIMEOUT_EN clear, ADDR slave field and TX_DATA, through one store function behind an independent write allowlist (bsd/dev/sweet_chg_i2c.c i2c_wr_allow[]); never CONF, TIMING_FS1-3, TRAILIG_CTL, USI_CON, SW_RST, SW_CONF, clocks or pads. No chip register is written: the only byte sent to a chip is the register address of a read. Pass: PMIC 0x66 regs 0x00/0x01/0x60, TCPC 0x25 regs 0x00-0x05 and 0x87, FG 0x36 reg 0x21 (+VCell/Current/RepSOC), charger 0x69 regs 0xB0-0xCC; stops if PMIC_ID != 0x3B or the FG DEVNAME high byte is not 0x62/0x63. Any timeout/NACK/error logs a SWEET CHG GAP line with the controller registers and stops ALL further transfers (no controller reset: its re-init is bring-up). Before every group the phase-1 gate state is re-read (sweet_chg_gate_still_open, new in sweet_chg.c) and must equal the open pattern, and the controller must still look as phase 1 saw it. ADT: soc.json chg_i2c -> /sweet-chg i-* properties. Applies after 0283. Host test: tools/test_chg_i2c.py.

